        "original_id": "faba372f-92e0-5dce-a105-99d41b9d41f4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: New York – New Jersey Line War\n- Places: disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey\n- Organizations: Province of New York assembly\n- Roles: Mayor of New York City, speaker\n- People: John Cruger Jr.\n- Places: Province of New York, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of New York existed from 1664 to 1776 as a British proprietary colony and later a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America.\n- The New York – New Jersey Line War, also called the N.J. Line War, consisted of skirmishes and raids from 1701 to 1765 along the disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey.\n- John Cruger Jr. was born on July 18, 1710, and died on December 27, 1791.\n- John Cruger Jr. served as speaker of the Province of New York assembly.\n- John Cruger Jr. was the 41st Mayor of New York City.",
